If we buy $K$ units, the cost is roughly $\sum_{j=1}^K (2j-1) P_{min} \approx K^2 P_{min}$.
So $K^2 P_{min} \approx M \implies K \approx \sqrt{M/P_{min}}$.
Since $M \le 10^{18}$ and $P_{min} \ge 1$, $K$ can be up to $10^9$.
We cannot iterate through all units.

